---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Project Roadmap & Phase Gates" activeNav="roadmap">
  <div style="max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <div style="margin-bottom: 3.5rem;">
      <h1 style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem); font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: -0.025em; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
        Project Roadmap & Gates
      </h1>
      <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.6;">
        Trooth grows through strict, transparent phase gates tied to cost constraints and verified user demand (CLAUDE.md section 9).
      </p>
      <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 0.85rem;">
        Every gate has three parts and all three have to clear. <strong>Technical</strong> is a test that passes or fails. <strong>Commercial</strong> is a number. <strong>Desirability</strong> is a question with a yes or no answer, asked of somebody outside this project, and it is the only one of the three that cannot be satisfied by working harder.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Phases Timeline -->
    <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2rem; margin-bottom: 4rem;">
      <!-- Phase 0 -->
      <div class="card" style="border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-green);">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--text-main);">
            Phase 0: The Benchmark
          </h2>
          <span class="badge">In progress</span>
        </div>
        <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-subtle); margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          Timeline: Weeks 1-3 | Cost Ceiling: &lt; $5/month (Actual: $0.00)
        </div>
        <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          Ships the routing catalog of 5 verified sources, the connector registry, the snapshot and diff jobs, this site and the free Console, and Modafied's emblems rendered as they come.
        </p>
        <div style="background-color: var(--bg-surface); padding: 0.85rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.88rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">
          <strong>Gate to proceed.</strong>
          <div style="margin-top: 0.5rem;"><strong style="color: var(--accent-green);">Technical:</strong> the archive persists across two consecutive cron runs, 5 sources are merged, and Modafied is grading at least 3 with its manifest pinned and verifying.</div>
          <div style="margin-top: 0.35rem;"><strong style="color: var(--accent-green);">Commercial:</strong> spend stays under $5 a month.</div>
          <div style="margin-top: 0.35rem;"><strong style="color: var(--accent-green);">Desirability:</strong> the fresh-agent test passes, and one outside reader asks for a source to be added.</div>
          <div style="margin-top: 0.6rem; color: var(--text-muted);">Not satisfied yet: the snapshot cron writes to a runner disk it then discards, so no archive is accumulating.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Phase 1 -->
      <div class="card" style="border-left: 4px solid var(--primary); background-color: #13223f;">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--primary);">
            Phase 1: The Free Pipe
          </h2>
          <span class="badge badge-blue">Active / Next Up</span>
        </div>
        <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-subtle); margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          Timeline: Weeks 4-8 | Cost Ceiling: &lt; $20/month
        </div>
        <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          Ships the single data connector: TypeScript Cloudflare Worker REST API and thin MCP server implementing the exact six tools. Every fetch returns an Ed25519 signed envelope with provenance.
        </p>
        <div style="background-color: var(--bg-surface); padding: 0.85rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.88rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">
          <strong style="color: var(--primary);">Gate to proceed.</strong>
          <div style="margin-top: 0.5rem;"><strong style="color: var(--primary);">Technical:</strong> p95 under 400ms on the quickstart path, and every response carries an envelope with its rejected candidates listed.</div>
          <div style="margin-top: 0.35rem;"><strong style="color: var(--primary);">Commercial:</strong> 25 distinct weekly active callers, at least one an autonomous production tool.</div>
          <div style="margin-top: 0.35rem;"><strong style="color: var(--primary);">Desirability:</strong> one external developer replaces a direct API call with Trooth, and says why.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Phase 2 -->
      <div class="card" style="border-left: 4px solid var(--border);">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--text-main);">
            Phase 2: Paid Tier & Immutability
          </h2>
          <span class="badge">Gated</span>
        </div>
        <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-subtle); margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          Timeline: Weeks 9-14 | Cost Ceiling: &lt; $50/month
        </div>
        <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          Ships Stripe metered billing, Pro tier ($39/mo for 100k requests), 1-year historical snapshot replay, schema change webhooks, and append-only Merkle transparency log anchored into Bitcoin via OpenTimestamps.
        </p>
        <div style="background-color: var(--bg-surface); padding: 0.85rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.88rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">
          <strong style="color: var(--text-muted);">Gate to proceed.</strong>
          <div style="margin-top: 0.5rem;"><strong>Technical:</strong> the same query replayed with <code>as_of</code> returns byte-identical data and a byte-identical envelope hash.</div>
          <div style="margin-top: 0.35rem;"><strong>Commercial:</strong> a first paying customer. No new cost-bearing feature is built until this is met.</div>
          <div style="margin-top: 0.35rem;"><strong>Desirability:</strong> that customer renews or expands.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Phase 3 -->
      <div class="card" style="border-left: 4px solid var(--border);">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--text-main);">
            Phase 3: The Provider Marketplace
          </h2>
          <span class="badge">Future</span>
        </div>
        <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-subtle); margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          Timeline: After Phase 2 Gate | Cost Model: Scales with revenue
        </div>
        <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          Allows external data owners to list feeds, filters, or analysis layers. Trooth meters calls and handles automated payouts with a platform take rate. Grading stays with Modafied, listed feeds included.
        </p>
        <div style="background-color: var(--bg-surface); padding: 0.85rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.88rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">
          <strong style="color: var(--text-muted);">Gate to proceed.</strong>
          <div style="margin-top: 0.5rem;"><strong>Technical:</strong> a provider's feed gets a Modafied scorecard without hand-holding.</div>
          <div style="margin-top: 0.35rem;"><strong>Commercial:</strong> 3 providers listed and 1 paid feed actively transacting.</div>
          <div style="margin-top: 0.35rem;"><strong>Desirability:</strong> a provider cites their scorecard publicly, without being asked.</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Phase 4 -->
      <div class="card" style="border-left: 4px solid var(--border);">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--text-main);">
            Phase 4: Specialized Verticals & Licensing
          </h2>
          <span class="badge">Future</span>
        </div>
        <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-subtle); margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          Timeline: After Phase 3 Gate
        </div>
        <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          Regulatory data slices (openFDA MAUDE medical device reports), sports feeds graded against settled game outcomes, and licensed historical revision datasets.
        </p>
        <div style="background-color: var(--bg-surface); padding: 0.85rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.88rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">
          <strong style="color: var(--text-muted);">Gate to proceed.</strong>
          <div style="margin-top: 0.5rem;"><strong>Technical:</strong> the vertical ships on the same envelope with no special case in the pipe.</div>
          <div style="margin-top: 0.35rem;"><strong>Commercial:</strong> decided on revenue.</div>
          <div style="margin-top: 0.35rem;"><strong>Desirability:</strong> a vertical user asks for a second feed.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Where Trooth sits -->
    <section class="card" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">Where Trooth sits</h3>
      <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
        Trooth is one layer of three, and the split is deliberate. Trooth fetches external data and
        wraps it in a provenance envelope. <a href="https://alexchouck-hash.github.io/kourob/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">KouroB</a>
        answers repeated questions above it, by replaying short graded chains of small models rather
        than calling a frontier model every time. <a href="https://alexchouck-hash.github.io/modafied-site/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Modafied</a>
        grades what both of them do, against named anchors, with open code.
      </p>
      <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.7;">
        Two of those layers route, and they route differently. Trooth decides which source answers a
        fetch, which is a lookup against a catalog. KouroB decides which models answer a query, which
        is a planning problem. Keeping them apart is why neither one can quietly become the other,
        and it is why the planner's failure modes are not the pipe's.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Kill / Pivot Rule -->
    <section class="card" style="border-color: rgba(244, 63, 94, 0.4); background-color: rgba(244, 63, 94, 0.05);">
      <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent-rose); margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
        Kill / Pivot Rule (CLAUDE.md section 9)
      </h3>
      <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.6;">
        If Phase 2 ends with zero paying customers and fewer than 50 weekly active keys, Trooth freezes at Phase 1, keeps the public benchmark running for brand reputation at under $10/month, and documents the retrospective in public experiments. We do not burn capital without proven market pull.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
